WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.790 --> 00:00:04.320
Catalysts. Electrochemistry. Process engineering.

2
00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.357
Hi, I'm Ayush Suryawanshi,

3
00:00:06.357 --> 00:00:09.730
a chemical engineer with hands-on work in all three.

4
00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:12.681
I'm a chemical engineer from IIT Madras,

5
00:00:12.681 --> 00:00:16.120
and right now I'm a Management Trainee at LOXIM Industries.

6
00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:17.610
Let me show you what I do.

7
00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.060
It starts with the catalyst.

8
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.684
For my master's thesis,

9
00:00:21.684 --> 00:00:24.799
I added bismuth to platinum to stop carbon monoxide

10
00:00:24.799 --> 00:00:27.180
poisoning it in formic acid fuel cells.

11
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.280
At NTNU in Norway, when the synthesis proved unsafe to scale, I reworked it.

12
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.730
Then I put it to the test.

13
00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.710
In three-electrode cells, I measure what a catalyst really does.

14
00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:43.508
My best one held on to nearly 93% of its current after an hour.

15
00:00:43.508 --> 00:00:45.780
Commercial platinum? About 58%.

16
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.990
But a good catalyst is only half the story.

17
00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:53.707
In Norway, I also worked with industry partners on a boiler retrofit:

18
00:00:53.707 --> 00:00:56.980
kinetic models, equipment sizing, safety and cost.

19
00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.860
At LOXIM, it all came together.

20
00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.317
On a two-month project,

21
00:01:01.317 --> 00:01:04.487
I mapped where a dye plant's effluent-treatment cost goes,

22
00:01:04.487 --> 00:01:06.072
and compared electrochemical,

23
00:01:06.072 --> 00:01:08.860
membrane and crystallisation routes with suppliers.

24
00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:09.727
The outcome:

25
00:01:09.727 --> 00:01:13.622
a proposed treatment train that turns the waste salt into a product,

26
00:01:13.622 --> 00:01:16.600
at a modelled operating cost about two-thirds lower.

27
00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:20.920
I handed it over with a validation roadmap for the next stage of evaluation.

28
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.720
So, what am I looking for next?

29
00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:27.609
A role in process engineering, electrochemistry, or catalysis.

30
00:01:27.609 --> 00:01:29.780
Any one of them, or where they meet.

31
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.576
Whether your team needs a process engineer, an electrochemist,

32
00:01:33.576 --> 00:01:36.700
or someone who can bridge the two, I'd love to hear from you.

33
00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:37.700
Let's talk.
